{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11187": {
      "title": "Research Compliance Coordinator",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Research Compliance Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Research Compliance Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Research Compliance Coordinator Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Grants & Sponsored Projects-Metro Hiring Manager: Carolynn Julien Hiring Manager Title: Associate Provost for Research and Sponsored Projects College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 23 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $48,396.--$53,354. General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Office of Grants and Sponsored Projects ( GSP ) reports to the University Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and serves as Fairleigh Dickinson University’s central resource for sponsored research and externally funded activities. GSP partners with faculty, staff, and University leadership across the full lifecycle of sponsored projects, from identifying funding opportunities and developing and submitting competitive proposals through award administration, project management, and closeout. The Office also supports the University’s research compliance infrastructure and promotes responsible research practices by interpreting and implementing sponsor requirements, University policies and procedures, and applicable federal and state regulations. Through guidance, education, training, and direct support, GSP helps strengthen institutional re-search capacity, facilitate successful sponsored activities, and minimize institutional risk. Rooted in a culture of connection and collaboration, the Office of Grants and Sponsored Projects is the focal point for research and grant-related activities at Fairleigh Dickinson University. We are focused on how we support one another and how we show up for our FDU community. Together, we strive to advance our mission to transform sponsored research and serve as agents of positive change. The Research Compliance Coordinator reports to the Associate Provost for Research and Sponsored Projects and supports the administration of Fairleigh Dickinson University’s research compliance programs. The Coordinator serves as the primary administrative contact for the University’s Institutional Review Board ( IRB ), manages the day-to-day workflow of human subjects research submissions, conducts preliminary reviews to assess completeness and identify the appropriate review pathway, and coordinates review by the IRB Chair or designated IRB members. The Coordinator also provides administrative and operational support for the University’s broader research compliance activities, including biosafety, animal care and use, conflict of interest, responsible conduct of research, research security, export control, and related research compliance training and requirements. The position maintains accurate records, communicates requirements and review outcomes, and supports the development and implementation of efficient, transparent research compliance processes. As a member of the Research and Sponsored Projects team, the Coordinator participates in the Office’s cross-training model and may provide support across research administration functions based on workload and institutional needs. This may include assisting with proposal preparation and submission, sponsored project administration, internal funding programs, research-related initiatives, and other pre-award or post-award activities. This is an early-career professional position that provides an opportunity to develop broad expertise in research compliance, sponsored projects, and research administration. Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree required in a work-related field from an accredited institution. 2. Minimum of 1-3 years of work-related experience required. Preferably in higher education, research, healthcare, legal or regulatory administration, compliance, or a related environment. Familiarity with human subjects research, research administration, regulatory compliance, electronic workflow systems, or research compliance training programs such as CITI is a plus. 3. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with excellent attention to detail and the ability to work accurately with complex information. 4. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate professionally and effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, committee members, and other constituents. 5. Ability to manage multiple assignments, deadlines, records, and workflows simultaneously in a service-oriented environment. 6. Ability and willingness to learn and apply federal regulations, institutional policies, and established procedures and to exercise sound judgment regarding when matters require consultation or escalation. 7. Strong computer skills, including word processing, spreadsheet and data management applications, and demonstrated ability to learn electronic research administration and compliance systems. 8. Ability to exercise discretion and appropriately handle sensitive and confidential information. 9. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively as a team member with a positive, flexible, and service-oriented approach; interact effectively and professionally with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, roles, and levels of the University; adapt to changing priorities and responsibilities; and be receptive to feedback and coaching. 10. Prior professional research compliance experience is not required. The position provides an opportunity to develop broad expertise in research compliance and research administration. 11. Valid driver’s license and accessibility to a car for travel between campuses. 12. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 10/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11185": {
      "title": "Associate General Counsel",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Associate General Counsel Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Associate General Counsel Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Associate General Counsel Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: General Counsel-Metro Hiring Manager: Jennifer Soyka Hiring Manager Title: General Counsel & Chief Comp Officer & Sec of Brd. College: Position Type: Executive Grade: Executive FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $150,000.--$200,000. General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Associate General Counsel is a senior attorney in the Office of the General Counsel who provides timely, practical, and strategic legal advice to university trustees, senior leaders, academic and administrative units, and affiliated entities. Reporting to the General Counsel or a designated Deputy General Counsel, the position manages a broad portfolio of legal matters in a complex, highly regulated environment and helps advance the university’s academic, research, health, business, student-life, and intercollegiate athletics missions. The Associate General Counsel works collaboratively across the institution, exercises sound independent judgment, manages risk without unnecessarily impeding innovation, and may supervise attorneys, legal professionals, outside counsel, or project teams. Required Qualifications: 1. Juris Doctor degree from a law school accredited by the American Bar Association required. 2. Must be a member in good standing of any U.S. state bar. If not currently admitted to the New Jersey State Bar, the successful candidate must obtain admission via reciprocity or examination within six (6) months of their start date. 3. A minimum of four years of progressively responsible legal experience after law school in a law firm, government agency, corporate legal department, higher-education legal office, not-for-profit, or comparable setting required. 4. Demonstrated experience independently managing complex matters and providing practical legal advice to senior leaders and sophisticated clients required. 5. Substantial experience in one or more areas relevant to a university, such as higher education, athletics, employment, litigation and investigations, governance, research, privacy, intellectual property, real estate, or complex commercial transactions is preferred. 6. Experience advising a large, decentralized, university or similarly complex nonprofit organization including advising boards, presidents, provosts, deans, or other executive leaders preferred. 7. Experience with college athletics including NCAA Division I athletics, conference rules, or legal issues affecting student-athletes and collegiate sports preferred. .8. Familiarity with the laws and regulatory environment of the New Jersey and the northeastern United States preferred and a demonstrated ability to learn new areas of law quickly, as needed. 9. Excellent legal research, analysis, drafting, negotiation, counseling, and oral and written communication skills to effectively communicate with both legal and nonlegal audiences. 10. Excellent relationship-management skills with the ability to negotiate, collaborate and communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing, including being able to explain legal terms and recommend strategies to stakeholders. 11. Demonstrated sound judgment, discretion, integrity, and ability to protect confidential and privileged information. 12. Ability to manage competing priorities, respond effectively to urgent matters, collaborate across diverse functions, and work independently with limited supervision. 13. Ability to work effectively in a diverse academic community. 14. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 10/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
