    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11161": {
      "title": "Admin Asst for Center for Academic Adv &amp; Student Success",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Admin Asst for Center for Academic Adv &amp; Student Success Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Admin Asst for Center for Academic Adv & Student Success Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Admin Asst for Center for Academic Adv & Student Success Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Academic Advising & Student Success-Metro Hiring Manager: Andrea Mosca Hiring Manager Title: Director, Center for Academic Advising & Student Success College: Position Type: Staff Grade: 11 FLSA: Non-Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $33,930.87--$42,953.34 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Administrative Assistant to the Center for Academic Advising and Student Success ( CAASS ) serves as the Office Manager and provides advanced and diversified administrative support primarily to the Campus Director of CAASS (Florham or Metro) and secondarily to the academic advisors and other staff housed within the Center. Primary Center responsibilities include, serving as initial point of contact for students, parents, faculty, and administrators; providing administrative support for CAASS staff, programs and initiatives; communicating office policies, procedures and practices to students, University personnel and the community-at-large; researching information; overseeing and/or participating in the coordination and maintenance of all office files, including confidential student records; completing purchase requisitions and maintaining associated budget records; and serving as the Advisement Center’s liaison to academic departments for matters and issues related to the operation of the Advisement Center. The incumbent will also work closely with the Director and academic advisors on creating and maintaining the curriculum checksheets used by all Departments on the Florham or Metro campus. The incumbent is expected to interface with students, parents, and the University community in a highly professional manner, using independent judgment and discretion. This position is required to maintain confidentiality of proprietary and private information and a customer-service focus while carrying out job responsibilities and will conduct business in a manner that will uphold the integrity and reputation of Fairleigh Dickinson University. This position maintains a thorough working knowledge of and adheres to the policies, regulations, and procedures of the University. Required Qualifications: 1. High School degree required. 2. Completion of courses and/or training related to secretarial, general office, administrative and computer skills or demonstrated equivalency through work experience, preferably in an academic environment preferred. 3. A minimum of two years of administrative experience, preferably in a complex academic environment, including office oversight responsibilities, experience with budget maintenance, and demonstrating strong organizational effectiveness. 4. Excellent human relations and oral and written communication skills with sensitivity to student needs. 5. Ability to handle a high volume of phone calls and personal contacts with students, faculty and staff in a professional manner and communicate clearly and concisely. 6. Computer proficiency for word processing, spreadsheets, data management, and e-mail. Knowledge of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), database software, and web navigation. Knowledge of Datatel and Canvas not required, but a plus. 7. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 08/14/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11159": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Finance",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Associate Vice President for Finance Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Associate Vice President for Finance Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Associate Vice President for Finance Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Financial Affairs, VP's Office-Metro Hiring Manager: Lisa Clarke Hiring Manager Title: Interim Vice President for Finance College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 34 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $160,000--$180,000 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Treasurer, the Associate Vice President for Finance serves as the senior operational leader for the Finance Division and is responsible for the effective day-to-day management of the University’s accounting, financial reporting, budgeting, purchasing/procurement, audit coordination, tax and regulatory compliance, and related finance operations. The Associate Vice President translates institutional financial strategy into disciplined processes, reliable forecasts, timely reporting, strong internal controls, and effective financial management across the University. The position works closely with the Vice President for Finance and Treasurer to implement the annual budget, long-range financial plan, scenario analyses, and the financial components of strategic initiatives and partnerships. In a challenging higher education environment, the Associate Vice President is expected to be a hands-on leader who strengthens accountability, develops staff, improves processes and systems, and provides responsive, decision-useful financial support while maintaining appropriate stewardship and control. Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree required in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field. CPA certification required; Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field preferred. 2. Minimum of eight years of progressively responsible accounting, budgeting, financial reporting, or financial management experience required, including significant supervisory or management responsibility. Experience in higher education, a not-for-profit organization, or public accounting serving complex not-for-profit or higher education clients strongly preferred. 3. Demonstrated knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles, financial statement preparation, audit requirements, internal controls, budgeting, forecasting, cash management, tax and regulatory compliance, and financial reporting in a complex organization. 4. Demonstrated ability to manage an annual budget process, develop forecasts and financial models, analyze variances and trends, and translate financial information into practical recommendations for operating leaders. 5. Demonstrated success improving financial processes, controls, reporting, and systems. Experience with enterprise financial systems, preferably Ellucian, and advanced proficiency with Excel and financial reporting/analytics tools required. 6. Strong leadership, communication, and management skills, including the ability to develop staff, establish accountability, manage competing priorities, and work effectively with diverse academic and administrative constituencies in a resource-constrained and changing environment. 7. Ability to comprehend, interpret, and apply policies, procedures, laws, regulations, accounting standards, and institutional guidelines; ability to identify risk and exercise sound judgment in complex situations. 8. Ability to handle matters of a highly confidential and sensitive nature with discretion, professionalism, and sound judgment. 9. Valid driver’s license and accessibility to transportation for travel between campuses. 10. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 09/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11146": {
      "title": "Advisement Counselor (Bilingual)",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Advisement Counselor (Bilingual) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Advisement Counselor (Bilingual) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Advisement Counselor (Bilingual) Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Academic Advising & Student Success-Metro Hiring Manager: Andrea Mosca Hiring Manager Title: Director, Center for Academic Advising & Student Success College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 25 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $55,000-60,000 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The incumbent reports to the Director of the Advising Center on the Metropolitan Campus. The primary responsibilities of this position are to engage in all student advisement service, in Spanish, of students in the HACER and Puerta al Futuro programs of FDU’s Hispanic Center as well as for undergraduate students in Becton College, and the School of Psychology and Counseling. Provides assistance and support for Open Houses, Orientation, and Admitted Student Day programs. This advisor will work closely in delivering advising services to all members of the college community, in addition to working closely with other support offices on the students’ behalf. Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree with two – three years’ experience in advising and student program planning or equivalent combination required. Master’s Degree in counseling, student personnel administration or related field highly desirable. 2. Fluency and literacy in both Spanish and English (preferably native speaker of one of these languages with superior-level proficiency, as described in the ACTFL Proficiency Guidelines at https://www.actfl.org/resources/actfl-proficiency-guidelines-2012, in the other). 3. Must have an understanding of retention and first year student issues in general and with special focus on issues of first-generation and immigrant students. 4. Ability to learn extensive requirements, policies and procedures and explain them to students and their family members as well as community members, in both English and Spanish. 5. Excellent oral, written, and listening skills in both English and Spanish with a sensitivity to student needs. 6. Familiarity with the North Jersey Hispanic Community and its cultural practices. 7. Excellent organizational, problem solving and time management skills. 8. Computer proficiency, including knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, Access, database software and web navigation. Experience with student databases, self-service, advise and degree audit systems is desirable. 9. Willing and able to work non-standard hours as required, including evenings, weekends and holidays. 10. Ability to maintain confidentiality in dealing with students, staff and faculty. 11. Ability to contribute to a supportive, team-oriented environment. 12. Willing and able to work non-standard hours as required, including evenings and weekends. 13. Valid driver’s license and accessibility to a car for travel to the Metropolitan Campus and/or off-campus locations as required. 14. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 09/04/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
