ture courses and corresponding recitation sections. The instructor is expected to lead in-person instruction to students and assess student learning through the assigning of homework sets, worksheets, quizzes, and exams. The instructor will be required to grade these assignments and provide the students with feedback in a timely manner. They will also need to assign student final grades for the course. Required Qualifications: Applicants are required to hold a Master’s degree or above in chemistry or closely related field. Teaching experience is required. Candidates with industrial experience are also welcome to apply. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae/resume. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 07/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
