      "title": "Adjunct Faculty for Electrical Energy Conversion-Fall 2026",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Faculty for Electrical Energy Conversion-Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Faculty for Electrical Energy Conversion-Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Faculty for Electrical Energy Conversion-Fall 2026 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Dept. of Engineering and Science-Metro Hiring Manager: Kalyan Mondal Hiring Manager Title: Interim Director, Engineering and Science College: Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $4,400. General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Temporary Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: EENG_4375 Electrical Energy Conversion (3 Credits) General considerations of electromagnetic phenomena and magnetic circuits. Exercises with ferromagnetic loops and air gap. Transformer theory—equivalent circuits and phasors. Regulation and efficiency evaluation, rotating machinery, DC and three phase systems. Power relationships, operating characteristics. This course also includes a 1 contact hour of lab and as such is a 4 contact hours course. Required Qualifications: Minimum qualifications: A MS in Electrical Engineering with experience in teaching college-level Electric Machines course/s. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 03/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
