    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10592": {
      "title": "School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: School of Education-Metro Hiring Manager: Kathryn Spence Hiring Manager Title: Director, School of Education College: Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: No Response Salary: $135.00/Observation General Benefits n/a Status: Part-Time Months Worked: Job Summary: Fairleigh Dickinson University is seeking experienced educators to serve as clinical supervisors for graduate students in School of Education programs. For the fall semester, this role will support either paraprofessionals participating in FDU’s PARE (Paraprofessional Alternate Route Educators) Grant Program or Reading Specialists employed in schools throughout New Jersey. PARE Program Supervisors will support paraprofessionals in Bergen County, New Jersey transitioning into certified teaching roles by providing mentorship, observation, and evaluation during their clinical practicum placements. Supervisors will serve as liaisons between FDU and partnering schools, ensuring alignment between university expectations and school-based practices. Supervisors will conduct observations using FDU approved inventories. This is a meaningful opportunity to contribute to the development of future educators. Key Responsibilities Observe and evaluate paraprofessional teacher or Reading Specialist candidates during their practicum placements. Conduct goal-setting, pre-observation, and post-observation conferences at least every other week during the semester ( PARE ) or three times during the semester (Reading Specialist). Provide timely, constructive written and verbal feedback. Collaborate regularly with cooperating teachers and school personnel. Submit observation reports, competency inventories, and final evaluations using FDU’s data management system. Attend required orientations, training sessions, and supervisor meetings. Communicate consistently with the Director of Field Placement and respective graduate program directors regarding candidate progress and concerns. Support candidates in integrating university curriculum with school-based practices. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Education or a closely related field. Minimum of 5 years of teaching or administrative experience. Demonstrated expertise in mentoring or supervising educators. Experience working in urban or underserved school settings. Strong communication and organizational skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and equitable learning environment Preferred Qualifications: Experience supervising paraprofessionals or non-traditional teacher candidates. Familiarity with remote teaching tools and practices. Prior involvement in grant-funded educational programs. Hours Worked Posting Date: 09/05/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10460": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Philosophy – Metro and /or Florham Campuses Fall 2025",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor of Philosophy – Metro and /or Florham Campuses Fall 2025 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor of Philosophy – Metro and /or Florham Campuses Fall 2025 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor of Philosophy – Metro and /or Florham Campuses Fall 2025 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: English, Philosophy & Humanities-Metro Hiring Manager: Matthieu Boyd Hiring Manager Title: Chair, Humanities College: Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $1,000 per credit; $3,000 for 3 credit section General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Part-Time Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: The School of the Humanities (part of the Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education) at Fairleigh Dickinson University ( https://www.fdu.edu/ ) is looking for part-time (adjunct) faculty to teach in-person sections of Ethics and other Philosophy courses starting in Fall 2025. Sections are all 3 credit hours (150 minutes of class per week) and meet Monday-Thursday, Tuesday-Friday, or as a double block on different days including Wednesday. You can teach one course or several. If you are successful in the position, teaching should be available every semester going forward. Our immediate need for Fall 2025 (semester starting August 25, see https://www.fdu.edu/academics/academic-calendar/2025-2026/ ) is for sections of Ethics, Intro to Philosophy, and Ethical Issues in the Movies. Most of these are scheduled to meet in person on our Florham Campus at 285 Madison Avenue, Madison NJ, and on our Metro Campus at 1000 River Road, Teaneck NJ, but for an exceptional candidate we could explore moving them online (we already have offers to teach online and would much prefer in person). There may be a few opportunities to teach sections that are already designated synchronous online. Ethics is a Gen Ed requirement at FDU : all our students have to take it. We are looking for someone who can teach the subject responsibly, from a philosophical standpoint, but in a way that is interactive, engaging, relevant to students’ lives, and maybe even fun. Intro to Philosophy is for our Humanities majors as well as the Gen Ed requirement in Humanities. All sections are expected to have 10–30 students and to involve significant discussion, not just lecture. The ideal candidate would have a PhD in Philosophy with specialization in ethics. We will be happy to consider you if you have any advanced degree in Philosophy or a related field, even if you are currently in graduate school, as long as you have experience with ethics or moral philosophy and can show some evidence of excellence in teaching. If you have a background in Theology or religious instruction, you are welcome to apply as long as you appreciate that FDU is not religiously affiliated and any teaching you do for us should not advance any particular religious viewpoint. Questions? Email Matthieu Boyd ( mwboyd@fdu.edu ), chair of Humanities. Required Qualifications: Advanced degree (PhD preferred, Master’s acceptable) in Philosophy or a related field. Coursework, teaching, or professional experience involving ethics or moral philosophy. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 07/08/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10321": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Information and Technological Literacy--METRO--2025",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Faculty of Information and Technological Literacy--METRO--2025 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Faculty of Information and Technological Literacy--METRO--2025 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Faculty of Information and Technological Literacy--METRO--2025 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Library-Metro Hiring Manager: Ana Fontoura Hiring Manager Title: University Librarian College: No Response Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: 3 credit course $3,000. General Benefits Status: Part-Time Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: A Master’s degree holder in Library and/or Information Science is needed to teach one or more 3-credit section(s) of INTEC1111: Technological and Information Literacy in fall 2024. The goal of this course is to assist students in acquiring confidence and proficiency in the technological and information literacy concepts of seeking, evaluating, managing, and using the wealth of information currently available in print, media, and online with digital tools. This course is designed to fulfill the General Education requirements for technology and information literacy. The candidate must have experience with information literacy, technological literacy, and various technology tools including but not limited to Microsoft Office Suite and library databases. The candidate is expected to impart hands-on knowledge to students in a computer lab classroom setting, following the profession’s standards and best practices. The candidate needs to conduct students learning outcome assessment and submit a report at the end of the course for accreditation purposes. Available class sessions are: Florham – MTh 1-2:15pm and TF 1-2:15pm; Metro – MTh 1-2:15pm and TF 1-2:15pm Required Qualifications: 1. MLS from an ALA accredited school or advanced degree in information science. 2. Demonstrable experience teaching information and technology literacy preferred. 3. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills with strong human relations skills. 4. Must have advanced knowledge of computer software/hardware operations, email, and web interface. 5. Ability to work with diverse faculty, staff, and students. 6. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked MTh 1-2:15pm and TF 1-2:15pm; Posting Date: 07/22/2024 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11207": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Chemistry Lab---Metro Campus -- Spring 2027",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor of Chemistry Lab---Metro Campus -- Spring 2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor of Chemistry Lab---Metro Campus -- Spring 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor of Chemistry Lab---Metro Campus -- Spring 2027 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Chemistry, Biochemistry and Physics-Metro Hiring Manager: Justin Bogart Hiring Manager Title: Dept Chair Biochemistry, Chemistry & Physics College: Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $900.-$1,000. Per Contact Hour General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Temporary Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: The Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science at Fairleigh Dickinson University, Metro Campus, seeks an adjunct professor to teach laboratory courses in the fields of general chemistry, organic chemistry and/or the health sciences. The laboratory instructor will be expected to guide students through the performance of weekly pre-designed in-person laboratory experiments in the respective discipline as well as evaluate student notebooks and laboratory reports. The position will also involve the maintenance and supervision of a safe laboratory environment by ensuring chemicals and glassware are handled correctly, PPE is worn, and waste is cleaned up and stored properly. Required Qualifications: Applicants are required to hold a Master’s degree or above in chemistry or closely related field. Teaching experience is strongly preferred. Candidates with industrial experience are also welcome to apply. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae/resume. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 07/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11203": {
      "title": "Nursing Faculty Lecturer",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Nursing Faculty Lecturer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Nursing Faculty Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Nursing Faculty Lecturer Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Nursing and Allied Health Services-Metro Hiring Manager: Annie Rohan Hiring Manager Title: Dean and Professor College: Henry P. Becton College of Nursing and Allied Health Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Lecturer Salary: $75,000 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 9 Month Job Summary: The responsibilities of College of Nursing and Allied Health faculty include teaching and service. We seek a faculty member who can teach within a population focus or other area of expertise and is comfortable with didactic and clinical instruction, and the use of digital learning resources. Specific rank is dependent on unique experience and qualifications. The faculty member will be effective in teaching and mentoring diverse students; developing and implementing existing and new curricula; engaging in university service; and participating in accreditation-related processes. Required Qualifications: MINIMUM and PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Required: An earned master’s degree in nursing. 2. Required: Unencumbered New Jersey registered nurse (RN) license. 3. Preferred: Comfort with pediatric, newborn, and maternity care content. 4. Required: Demonstrated teaching effectiveness. 5. Required: Proficiency in the use of computer systems for spreadsheets, word processing, internet, videoconferencing, and e-mail. 6. Required: Ability to manage sensitive issues with decorum and confidentiality. 7. Required: Well organized, independent, and collaborative in carrying out responsibilities. NOTE : Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 10/26/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11212": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Foundational Math--Metro 2027",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor of Foundational Math--Metro 2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor of Foundational Math--Metro 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor of Foundational Math--Metro 2027 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Foundational Math-Metro Hiring Manager: Yeoah Kim Hiring Manager Title: Director, Foundational Math Program College: Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $1100-$1200 per credit depending on course enrollment General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Part-Time Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: | The Foundational Math Program of Becton College at Fairleigh Dickinson University is seeking to hire adjuncts in Mathematics to teach primarily foundational math courses including Algebra Skills, Comprehensive Mathematics, and College Algebra at the Metro Campus. Required Qualifications: | A Master’s degree in mathematics or closely related field. Teaching experience is a must. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. | Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 05/17/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
